  "summary_of_core_decisions": "The text defends a Husserlian reading of Sartre's Being and Nothingness, arguing that Sartre radicalizes Husserl by including consciousness itself in the phenomenal world of appearances. It distinguishes three senses in which consciousness is a nothing, reinterprets the ego as a constituted noematic unity, and concludes that this reading makes Sartre's controversial claims more plausible.",
